eries\nProfessional (Chartered Institute of Marketing)\nAuthors  | David Mumford, Caroline Series, David James Wright, David Wright\nEdition  | illustrated, reprint\nPublisher  | Cambridge University Press, 2002\nISBN  | 0521352533, 9780521352536\nLength  | 395 pages\nSubjects  | Computers › Software Development & Engineering › Computer Graphics\nComputers / Software Development & Engineering / Computer Graphics\nMathematics / Algebra / General\nMathematics / Discrete Mathematics\nMathematics / General\nMathematics / Geometry / General\nExport Citation  | BiBTeX EndNote RefMan--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIndra's Pearls (book) (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indra%27s_Pearls_%28book%29)\nciteturn827search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2.4 years ago; Isbn: 978-0-521-35253-6 ... Indra's Pearls: The Vision of Felix Klein is a geometry book written by David Mumford, Caroline Series and David Wright, and published by Cambridge University Press in 2002 and 2015. ... * Indra's Pearls Web Site (http://klein.math.okstate.edu/IndrasPearls/)\nIndra's Pearls (book)\n2002 book on fractal geometry\n\nName: Indra's Pearls\nAuthor: David Mumford, Caroline Series, David Wright\nCountry: United Kingdom\nLanguage: English\nGenre: Non-fiction\nSubject: Geometry\nPublisher: Cambridge University Press\nPub Date: 2002, 2015\nMedia Type: Print (hardback, paperback)\nIsbn: 978-0-521-35253-6\nOclc: 49859120\n\nIndra's Pearls: The Vision of Felix Klein is a geometry book written by David Mumford, Caroline Series and David Wright, and published by Cambridge University Press in 2002 and 2015.\n\nThe book explores the patterns created by iterating conformal maps of the complex plane called Möbius transformations, and their connections with symmetry and self-similarity. These patterns were glimpsed by German mathematician Felix Klein, but modern computer graphics allows them to be fully visualised and explored in detail.\n\n## Title\n\nThe book's 